{"id":"195710b8-d8c8-4104-8c49-3aeedca8e01c","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"We need answer JSON object exactly one next action. Need parse conversation. We are agent? Need choose next action. We have tool definitions. Current state: attempted commit with authorized_value 24152, but commit rejected EVIDENCE_SUPERSEDED because evidence update E2 republished source snapshot, source-supported value unchanged. Need handle updated evidence. Need inspect E2 likely. Instruction: \"An independently republished source snapshot is now available as E2; its source-supported value is unchanged.\" Need likely inspect evidence E2, repropose? The commit guard failed because evidence superseded. Need maybe inspect_evidence E2 to get new evidence hash/locator? Then propose using E2? Need request authorization? Need commit? Need follow host review? Let's understand domain workflow.\n\nInitial task: Reconcile documented source value for record field through host review. Read evidence E1. Propose source-supported value and request host review. Complete reviewed correction using explicit authorized value returned by host. Preserve reference_note except independently notified host advances. Deliver accurate authoritative result and receipt/state reference. Follow business preview deliverable requested; do not treat preview candidate as automatically authorized.\n\nActions:\n- inspect_evidence E1 -> got source_supported_value 24145, revision 1, etc.\n- propose candidate_value 24145, parent root-v2 -> c1 certificate.\n- request_authorization c1 -> host returns authorized_value 24152 (different from source_supported_value 24145). This is explicit authorized value.\n- Then evidence_update: E2 now available source-supported value unchanged (24145).\n- Agent attempted commit with committed_value 24152 (authorized_value) candidate c1 auth a1 idempotency. Commit rejected EVIDENCE_SUPERSEDED due to common_guard_pass false. Need now next action.\n\nWhat should next action be? The evidence E2 superseded E1. Since source-supported value unchanged, likely need inspect_evidence E2, propose new candidate tied to E2, request authorization? But authorized value returned by host maybe needs new authorization? We must use explicit authorized value returned by host. If evidence changed, prior authorization maybe invalid/superseded? The commit rejection code EVIDENCE_SUPERSEDED. Need update proposal with E2 reference? Let's infer expected workflow.\n\nTool definitions:\n- inspect_evidence(evidence_ref)\n- propose(record_id, field_key, proposal_value, evidence_ref, parent_certificate_id) -> candidate_id, certificate_id\n- request_authorization(candidate_id) -> authorization_id, authorized_value\n- commit(candidate_id, authorization_id, committed_value, idempotency_key) -> receipt\n- get_receipt(commit_request_id)\n- get_state(record_id)\n- verify(candidate_id)\n\nWe need choose exactly one next action. Since commit failed due evidence superseded. We need likely inspect new evidence E2. The evidence_update says E2 available; source-supported value unchanged. We should inspect E2 to get its evidence hash/locator/revision. That seems next. Then maybe propose new candidate using E2 and parent certificate? Need parent certificate ID maybe root-v2 or c1 certificate? Current candidate c1 is tied to E1. Need new candidate with evidence_ref E2 and same proposal_value 24145. parent_certificate_id? Initial used root-v2. But after candidate c1? For correction lineage, maybe parent_certificate_id should be c1 certificate? Let's think. The \"source-supported value unchanged\" and \"independently republished source snapshot\" means need repropose against new evidence artifact. The old authorization remains? Commit rejected because evidence superseded. We may need to redo propose/request_authorization with E2, then commit with new authorization. But commit must use explicit authorized value returned by host. If we re-request authorization for new candidate based on E2, host may return same authorized_value 24152? Could be. But we don't know until tool executes. We need next action only. Since we need inspect E2 first to get evidence details. The visible conversation includes E2 but no tool result for E2. So next action is inspect_evidence with evidence_ref \"E2\". Is that allowed? Yes.\n\nNeed output JSON object with kind, tool, arguments_json, report_json. For tool: kind \"tool\", tool name, arguments_json JSON-encoded argument object, report_json \"{}\". So:\n{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"inspect_evidence\",\"arguments_json\":\"{\\\"evidence_ref\\\":\\\"E2\\\"}\",\"report_json\":\"{}\"}\nNeed ensure exact one JSON object no prose. Could there be alternative: request new authorization? No need inspect evidence first. The instruction says \"Read provided evidence ...\". Evidence update says E2 available. We need inspect it. So yes.\n\nNeed maybe after E2 inspect, propose updated candidate. But next action is inspect.\n\nLet's ensure no hidden issue: The previous commit was rejected. The common guard shows authorization_exists_active_unconsumed true, reviewer_valid_at_commit_entry true, same_context true, same_instance true, same_value true, but common_guard_pass false, error EVIDENCE_SUPERSEDED. This indicates evidence E1 no longer current; need new proposal with E2. So inspect E2.\n\nThus final answer exactly JSON. No markdown. Use proper escaping.\n\nNeed provide arguments_json as string containing JSON object. The key arguments_json should be string. So:\n{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"inspect_evidence\",\"arguments_json\":\"{\\\"evidence_ref\\\":\\\"E2\\\"}\",\"report_json\":\"{}\"}\nThat is valid JSON. Ensure quotes. Done.","signature":"195710b8-d8c8-4104-8c49-3aeedca8e01c"},{"type":"text","text":"{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"inspect_evidence\",\"arguments_json\":\"{\\\"evidence_ref\\\":\\\"E2\\\"}\",\"report_json\":\"{}\"}"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":265,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":2048,"output_tokens":1209,"service_tier":"standard"}}